  "title": "Kellogg-Briand Pact",
  "summary": "Signed in Paris on 27 August 1928, this multilateral treaty renounced war as an instrument of national policy and called for peaceful settlement of disputes. It took effect on 24 July 1929 after the last ratification was deposited. Many reservations and no enforcement meant Britannica judges it ineffective.",
